{{!
    @template local_dimensions/course_card

    Course card component for displaying a single course in the grid.

    Context variables required:
    * courseid (int) - The course ID for AJAX loading
    * fullname (string) - The course full name, escaped by format_string (printed raw)
    * courseurl (string) - URL to the course view page
    * viewcoursestr (string) - Accessible label for the course link, plain text
    * locked (bool) - Whether the course is locked for the user
    * skeletonrows (array) - One entry per skeleton row drawn while the card body loads

    @copyright  2026 Anderson Blaine
    @license    http://www.gnu.org/copyleft/gpl.html GNU GPL v3 or later

    Example context (json):
    {
        "courseid": 42,
        "fullname": "Introduction to Programming",
        "courseurl": "/course/view.php?id=42",
        "viewcoursestr": "View course: Introduction to Programming",
        "locked": false,
        "skeletonrows": [{"row": true}, {"row": true}, {"row": true}]
    }
}}
<div class="col-md-6 col-lg-4 mb-4 local-dimensions-course-card-wrapper"
     data-courseid="{{courseid}}"
     data-filtervalues="{{filtervaluesjson}}">
    <div class="card h-100 {{#locked}}local-dimensions-card-locked{{/locked}}">
        <h3 class="card-header fw-bold">
            {{#locked}}
                <span class="text-muted">{{{fullname}}}</span>
            {{/locked}}
            {{^locked}}
                <a href="{{courseurl}}" aria-label="{{viewcoursestr}}">{{{fullname}}}</a>
            {{/locked}}
        </h3>
        {{! The skeleton stands for the card body competency_view.js draws: one timeline row per
            section the server counted (skeletonrows), a ring and a name each. The grid carries
            aria-busy and the one status line; the container's own aria-busy goes when its body
            arrives. }}
        <div class="local-dimensions-progress-container" data-courseid="{{courseid}}" aria-busy="true">
            <div class="local-dimensions-sk" aria-hidden="true">
                {{#skeletonrows}}
                <span class="local-dimensions-sk-row">
                    <span class="local-dimensions-sk-block local-dimensions-sk-block--ring"></span>
                    <span class="local-dimensions-sk-block local-dimensions-sk-block--line"></span>
                </span>
                {{/skeletonrows}}
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
